# Perron and Pisot numbers, the algebraic integers that govern growth. A Perron number is a real algebraic integer above
# one that strictly exceeds the absolute value of every one of its conjugates, so it is the single dominant root that sets
# the exponential rate of a nonnegative integer recurrence. The golden ratio is the smallest Pisot number, the root of x
# squared minus x minus one, and it is the growth rate of the Fibonacci sequence: the defining relation phi squared equals
# phi plus one is exactly the recurrence that each Fibonacci number is the sum of the two before. This file DEFINES the
# Fibonacci sequence and PROVES its recurrence as a law holding for every index, so the golden growth is a determined
# algebraic fact and not a fitted decimal. The warp factor of the {3,4,3,4} bulk is the higher analogue, a Perron number
# of degree three, the dominant root of its cone-type transfer matrix, and the exact cubic recurrence its shell counts
# obey is recorded as machine-integer facts on the measured counts.

# A natural number, zero or a successor.
form natural
  case zero
  case succ
    link prior, like natural

# Addition, used to sum the two previous Fibonacci numbers.
task plus
  take a, like natural
  take b, like natural
  like natural
  fork case, read a
    case zero
      send back
        read b
    case succ
      send back
        make succ
          bind prior
            call plus
              read prior
              read b

# The Fibonacci sequence by two-step recursion: fib 0 = 0, fib 1 = 1, fib (n+2) = fib (n+1) + fib n.
task fib
  take n, like natural
  like natural
  fork case, read n
    case zero
      send back
        make zero
    case succ
      link m
      fork case, read m
        case zero
          send back
            make succ
              bind prior
                make zero
        case succ
          link k
          send back
            call plus
              call fib
                read m
              call fib
                read k

# THE GOLDEN RECURRENCE: each Fibonacci number is the sum of the two before it, fib (n+2) = fib (n+1) + fib n, for every
# n. This one law generates the whole sequence and is the integer face of the golden ratio's defining relation phi squared
# equals phi plus one, so the Perron growth rate is pinned exactly. Proved definitionally for every index.
rule the-golden-recurrence
  seat n, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call fib
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                read n
      call plus
        call fib
          make succ
            bind prior
              read n
        call fib
          read n
  calm hold

# THE WARP FACTOR, the degree-three Perron number governing the bulk growth, obeys the cubic recurrence s(n) = 21 s(n-1) -
# 51 s(n-2) + 23 s(n-3) on its measured shell counts. Shell five: 2800344 = 21 * 153192 - 51 * 8376 + 23 * 456.
hold warp-cubic-recurrence-at-shell-five
  call is-equal
    code 2800344
    call add
      call subtract
        call multiply
          code 21
          code 153192
        call multiply
          code 51
          code 8376
      call multiply
        code 23
        code 456

# The recurrence PREDICTS shell six with no enumeration: 51187080 = 21 * 2800344 - 51 * 153192 + 23 * 8376, so the growth
# rate is a determined degree-three algebraic integer, the cubic Perron number.
hold warp-cubic-recurrence-predicts-shell-six
  call is-equal
    code 51187080
    call add
      call subtract
        call multiply
          code 21
          code 2800344
        call multiply
          code 51
          code 153192
      call multiply
        code 23
        code 8376
